    "body": "This makes sense to me, but note that `ElementInternals` would not be able to share the same hypothetical interface mixin as the various elements listed. Its operations/attributes are used to achieve the same outward effects and deliberately mirror that API, but their internal behavior definitions (associated getter steps, etc) are necessarily different. (A mixin “includes” the associated behavior definitions; it’s not just the declaration of the member signatures independent from their behavior.)",
